    "body": "## Security impact\n\nSeveral authenticated private-job workflows still loaded a job globally by numeric id before checking whether the caller was a participant. That let an outsider distinguish an existing private job from a nonexistent id through dispute creation, review creation/eligibility, and negotiated-cancellation endpoints.\n\n## Fix\n\n- resolve dispute creation through the existing participant-scoped pessimistic job lookup;\n- resolve review creation through the participant-scoped locked lookup and review eligibility through the participant-scoped read lookup;\n- resolve negotiated-cancellation reads and mutations through participant-scoped job lookups;\n- fail closed to the existing neutral job-not-found response when the authenticated user id is unavailable or the caller is not a participant;\n- stop outsider requests before lifecycle/status inspection, review state access, pending-cancellation access, escrow checks, notifications, or persistence.\n\n## Behavioral invariants\n\nAuthorized participants keep the existing lifecycle, duplicate, counterparty, blocking, expense and escrow semantics. Admin dispute resolution remains global/trusted and unchanged. No schema or financial-flow changes.\n\n## Tests\n\n- outsider dispute creation cannot reach the global job lock, dispute lookup, or escrow assertion;\n- outsider review creation/eligibility returns neutral not-found before review access;\n- outsider cancellation request/pending read returns neutral not-found before cancellation records are touched;\n- existing participant success/conflict flows remain covered.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all exact-head checks are green, `master` has not moved, branch is 0 behind, and the merged SHA is exactly the checked head SHA.",
